# W2 (run 2 of 2): the same audits-off hang shapes on c2-packed-tp4-best-ship-warm4 (best-ship with the in-trace sampler off and QWEN_FAST_M3_REQUEST_WARM=1). Soft, and placed just before Z: this profile is
# only for after the warm4 window proves the warm out, and it has no stall watch (a hang costs the whole smoke step), so run W only if the tp4/warm4 window passed; otherwise skip W1 and W2. READ: completion of both runs, every user at budget, c2_smoke_check clean, concurrent4_code_equal hashes equal to the BS runs' hashes.
# A hang or a hash difference is a finding recorded against warm4, not a stop. Duration (estimate): 45 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-ship-warm4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal
